==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-in the long run.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Prepositional phrase===
{{en-PP|head=in the [[long run]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} After a very long time; [[eventually]]; over a long period of time; more generally.
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1923
|author=w:John Maynard Keynes
|title=A Tract on Monetary Reform
|chapter=3
|page=80
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/tractonmonetaryr0000keyn/page/80
|passage=But this ''long run'' is a misleading guide to current affairs. '''In the long run''' we are all dead.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1951|author=w:Arthur C. Clarke|title=The Exploration of Space|page=111
|passage=If we have learned one thing from the history of invention and discovery, it is that, '''in the long run''' — and often in the short one — the most daring prophecies seem laughably conservative.}}

